Root cause:
The bug was caused by improper handling of the breadcrumbs IRQ and associated timers during the reset path of the Intel graphics driver. Specifically, the previous implementation did not adequately cancel the fake IRQ and hangcheck timers, which could lead to incorrect state restoration and potential missed interrupts. The patch addresses this by ensuring that both timers are canceled and the interrupt mask register (IMR) is sanitized, thereby preventing issues related to incomplete requests and ensuring proper IRQ handling during engine resets.
